<title>CHILE: Chile sees beef exports to Japan rising.</title>
<headline>Chile sees beef exports to Japan rising.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean beef exports to Japan could rise following a declaration by Japanese officials that Chile's cattle industry is free of foot and mouth disease, said Chile's Agriculture Minister Carlos Mladinic.</p>
<p>&quot;This recognition opens a market space of incalculable proportions which must be considered by the national beef industry in coming days,&quot; Mladinic told a news conference.</p>
<p>Chilean food exports to Japan, which include salmon and fruit, totalled just $120 million last year. No figures for beef exports were available.</p>
<p>Japan imported 660,000 tonnes of beef last year, up from 584,000 tonnes in 1994.</p>
